Subject: [PATCH 1/4] RISC-V: Implement riscv_macro_fusion_pair_p for ARC-V
 RHX-100 series.

This patch adds the macro-op fusion cases used by the ARC-V RHX-100 and
enables them in the tune_info (fusible_ops).  Fusion rules are collected in a
table and dispatched from riscv_macro_fusion_pair_p; each is gated by its own
RISCV_FUSE_* flag so a tune enables only the pairs its hardware supports.

Adjacent load/store fusion is prioritized: the other pairs are suppressed
until sched2 so double load/store opportunities are not broken up.

Fusion cases enabled for the RHX-100 (I1 -> I2):

  RISCV_FUSE_MULT_ADD       (riscv_fuse_mult_add)
      mul rd + add rd,rd,rs3; the add reads the mul result in the same dest
      (on RV64 the result may be sign-extended to DImode).
  RISCV_FUSE_LI_BRANCH      (riscv_fuse_li_branch)
      li rd + conditional branch that uses rd.
  RISCV_FUSE_LI_STORE       (riscv_fuse_li_store)
      li rt + store of rt.
  RISCV_FUSE_LUI_ST         (riscv_fuse_lui_st)
      lui + store (either order).
  RISCV_FUSE_LUI_LD         (riscv_fuse_lui_ld)
      lui rd + load that uses rd as its base.
  RISCV_FUSE_LUI_LD_REV     (riscv_fuse_lui_ld_rev)
      load + lui (reversed lui+ld), with distinct destinations.
  RISCV_FUSE_LS_UPDATE      (riscv_fuse_ls_update)
      load + addi, or addi + store, updating the base register.
  RISCV_FUSE_BFEXT          (riscv_fuse_bfext)
      slli rd,rs + srli rd,rd (bitfield extract).
  RISCV_FUSE_ADJACENT_LOAD  (riscv_fuse_adjacent_load)
      two loads, same base, offsets |off1-off2| == XLEN/8.
  RISCV_FUSE_ADJACENT_STORE (riscv_fuse_adjacent_store)
      two stores, same base, offsets |off1-off2| == XLEN/8.

riscv_fuse_bfext and riscv_fuse_lui_ld already existed; this patch adds the
other eight checkers and enables the full set above for the RHX-100.  The
memory pairs only fire after reload (reload_completed && !sched_fusion), which
is why they are deferred to sched2.

